# WEIGHTS AND CORPORA ARE NOT SOURCE. This directory is ~18 GB, of which 232 .ckpt files are the
# bulk (80 MB each) and data/ is a further 667 MB with single CSVs over 130 MB. GitHub rejects
# files above 100 MB outright, and a repo carrying model weights stops being diffable, which is
# the entire reason this commit exists: the untracked state blocked verification twice tonight --
# nobody could diff train_phaseA.py across a mid-session edit to establish whether a behavioural
# change had occurred, so a reproduction question had to be settled by numeric agreement instead.
ckpt_*/
*.ckpt
data/
*.jsonl
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-run stdout. logs/ (the rescued run logs that PROVE which device a run used) IS tracked --
# that is provenance, not noise, and its absence from the repo is what forced a device to be
# inferred from throughput earlier tonight.
logs_*.log
